  "details": "When using a gamepad in desktop mode, then clicking on the \"Controls\" tab under settings, the menu shows the options for SteamVR. Previously, this would show the controls for desktop mode with a graphic of a gamepad showing its mappings, like shown on [VRChat's official documentation page](https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/gamepad).\n\nThis may or may not be related to a problem where [the deadzones for gamepads are different from what they used to be](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/gamepad-deadzones-too-extreme-not-configurable)\n\nEdit: Some additional context that may be important - I found this out because I couldn't search for the \"Mouse Look Sensitivity\" option until I remembered I was using a controller. Putting down the controller and clicking on the Controls tab with the mouse button rather than Right Trigger shows the correct settings for Keyboard.\n\nEdit 2: I was recently reminded of this because I had to take my Steam Deck with me on a trip only to find out that I couldn't access the right settings page as the Deck itself registers as a SteamVR input source, and looking around was tedious as I had to push the stick very far to do a small rotation.",
